  "details": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: RDMA/uverbs: Validate wqe_size before using it in ib_uverbs_post_send (CVE-2026-45856)\n  * kernel: KVM: SVM: Fix page overflow in sev_dbg_crypt() for ENCRYPT path (CVE-2026-63794)\n  * kernel: futex: Fix race on the initial mm->futex.phash.ref allocation (CVE-2026-80775)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * Backport of protocol attribute to IP addresses (IFA_PROTO) [almalinux-9.8.z] (JIRA:AlmaLinux-169936)\n  * try_charge_memcg() refactor in kernel 5.14.0-687.36.1 causes premature memcg OOM with GiB of clean page cache present [almalinux-9.8.z] (JIRA:AlmaLinux-269060)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
